\ Regression for the AOT no-exit-loop hang.
\
\ A word whose every path loops back is an infinite loop with no return, the
\ shape of a server accept loop (lib/net/server.1z serve-loop). AOT emits it as
\ a native for(;;). Before the fix, the finalize emitted an unreachable trailing
\ RETURN after the loop, and the vendored ir_emit_c backend hung generating C
\ for that dead code, so the build never terminated.
\
\ Compiling interpreter-free proves the loop emits to native C with no fallback.
\ The word is referenced through an escaping quotation and dropped, so it is
\ compiled but never entered and the program itself terminates.

loop-forever: ( n -- ) [ 1 + loop-forever ] ;

[ loop-forever ] drop
"ok" print-line
